{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Lattice"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.strict_max_witness_not_oneBody","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.strict_max_witness_not_oneBody","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L94-L98","doc":"**And that functional is not one-body**, so the exclusion is exactly the one-body\npremise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.strict_max_realisable_two_body","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.strict_max_realisable_two_body","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**The hypothesis is load-bearing.** The measured ordering pattern — unlike pair strictly\nabove both like pairs — is realised by a two-body functional, so `not_pn_strict_max` is a\nstatement about one-body functionals and not a vacuous one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.chargeIndependent_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.chargeIndependent_const","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L69-L85","doc":"**Charge independence collapses the whole table.** On a two-element index set, a one-body\nfunctional with `f p p = f n n` is constant on all four ordered channels: charge independence\nand charge symmetry leave no room for an unlike-pair difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.not_pn_strictly_between","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.not_pn_strictly_between","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L61-L66","doc":"**Nor strictly between the like pairs**, in either orientation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.not_pn_strict_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.not_pn_strict_min","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L55-L59","doc":"**Nor strictly the smallest.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.not_pn_strict_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.not_pn_strict_max","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L48-L53","doc":"**The unlike pair cannot be strictly the largest.** With `f` the binding, the deuteron can\nnever be more bound than both the diproton and the dineutron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.pn_eq_like","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.pn_eq_like","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L38-L44","doc":"**The unlike pair is always tied to a like pair.** Right-dependent: `f p n = f n n`;\nleft-dependent: `f p n = f p p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.OneBody","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.OneBodyBondOrdering.OneBody","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/OneBodyBondOrdering.lean#L33-L36","doc":"A pair functional is **one-body** if it is a function of one argument only — the right\none (`V1`, `V2` placements) or the left one (`V3`, `V4`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}